   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in relation to authorizing\nthe New York Wine and Culinary Center or a wholly owned subsidiary to operate\nthe Finger Lakes Welcome Center; and authorizes the sale of cider",
    "basePrintNo": "S7904",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7904-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §101, ABC L",
    "lawSection": "Alcoholic Beverage Control Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7904\n\nSPONSOR: HELMING\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in\nrelation to authorizing the New York Wine and Culinary Center or a whol-\nly owned subsidiary to operate the Finger Lakes Welcome Center; and\nauthorizes the sale of cider\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends Section 101 of the Alcoholic Beverage Control Law Part\n(i) amended to include the ability to sell New York state produced\ncider.\n\nPart (iii) amended to include the ability to sell and serve cider at\nsuch events.\n\nAdded:\n\nPart (iv) permits the New York State Wine and Culinary Center, Inc. to\noperate, either directly or through a permit issued to a wholly owned\nsubsidiary, the Finger Lakes Welcome Center situated at the premises\nknown as the \"Existing Building Exhibit Finger Lakes Welcome Center\"\nwith the appropriate metes-and-bounds description.\n\nSection 2: Establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe New York Wine & Culinary Center (NYWCC) is a 501(c)(3) not-for-pro-\nfit organization that showcases New York's dynamic agriculture, craft\nbeverages, and culinary arts. In 2017, it was announced that the NYWCC\nwould partner with the state to help design the Finger Lakes Welcome\nCenter (FLWC) in Geneva, NY. The FLWC is one of ten such facilities\nbeing built around the state and will showcase locally sourced craft\nbeverages and foods. One of the unique ways the New York Wine and Culi-\nnary Center (NYWCC) will be able to provide a different experience at\nthe FLWC, is its ability to utilize its NYWCC's farm winery license.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
